# ============================================================
# DNSCrypt Smart Filter – module.prop
# Version: v1.4.0 (Global Edition)
# Last updated: 2026-10-08
# Author: gasciljh
# Repository: https://github.com/gasciljh/dnscrypt-proxy-webui
# ============================================================
# Purpose:
#   Magisk / KernelSU / APatch module definition file.
#
#   Read by the root manager during install and update.
#   The `versionCode` drives update detection:
#     newer versionCode → the manager offers an update.
#
# Fields:
#   id                — unique module identifier (a-z, 0-9, -, _)
#   name              — human-readable name (shown in the manager)
#   version           — SemVer string (matches VERSION file)
#   versionCode       — monotonic integer (see formula below)
#   author            — maintainer handle
#   description       — long description (shown in the manager)
#   updateJson        — URL to update.json (auto-update metadata)
#   minMagiskVersion  — minimum root-manager version
#   supportUrl        — issue tracker URL
#   donateUrl         — empty; the project accepts no donations
#
# versionCode formula:
#   versionCode = MAJOR × 1,000,000
#               + MINOR ×    10,000
#               + PATCH ×       100
#               + HOTFIX
#
#   For v1.4.0:
#     MAJOR = 1, MINOR = 4, PATCH = 0, HOTFIX = 0
#     → 1 × 1,000,000 + 4 × 10,000 + 0 × 100 + 0
#     → 1,040,000
#
#   Updated automatically by scripts/release.sh (and
#   scripts/release-patch.sh for PATCH releases). Do not edit
#   manually — the release script verifies the change and
#   rejects a mismatched versionCode.
#
# ⚠️ Warning:
#   Do NOT add spaces around `=`.
#   Do NOT add a trailing comment on the same line as a value.
#   The Magisk parser is strict about this.
#
# ⚠️ Language policy (Global edition):
#   This file's comments are English-only (project convention).
#   The WebUI itself is bilingual (English default + Arabic
#   toggle) — the `langToggle` button is present in all three
#   HTML pages (index.html, dashboard.html, offline.html), and
#   the user's preference is stored client-side in
#   localStorage['dnscrypt-lang']. See the description field
#   below for the exact wording used in the module manager.
#
# ⚠️ versionCode history (for reference):
#   v1.0.0 → 1000000
#   v1.1.0 → 1010000
#   v1.2.0 → 1020000
#   v1.2.1 → 1020100  (not released)
#   v1.3.0 → 1030000
#   v1.4.0 → 1040000  (this release)
#   v1.4.1 → 1040100  (next PATCH, if needed)
#   v1.5.0 → 1050000  (next MINOR)
#
# ============================================================
# v1.3.0 — Server-side refinements (documentation correction)
# ============================================================
#   The v1.3.0 release was originally documented as client-side
#   only (PWA install button + live status LED + DNS auto-start
#   fix). That description was incomplete: the release also
#   shipped server-side refinements that were not documented in
#   the module metadata. This revision corrects the record.
#
#   Server-side refinements shipped in v1.3.0:
#     • main.go:buildBackupInfo() now detects snapshots by the
#       presence of `.manifest.json` (SNAP-MANIFEST) instead of
#       by name pattern, and sorts them by mtime for
#       `last_backup_name` (SNAP-MTIME).
#     • functions.sh:rotate_backups() was rewritten to use the
#       same manifest-based detection (ROT-MANIFEST), the same
#       mtime sort (ROT-MTIME), and to preserve two additional
#       targets on top of the 21-newest window: the `.last_stable`
#       recovery pointer and the newest install snapshot
#       (ROT-PROTECT).
#     • service.sh gained a boot-path DNS auto-start: a bounded
#       wait for the WebUI to become ready (up to 60 s, checking
#       the watchdog token file + the WebUI TCP port) followed by
#       a direct POST /api/ensure_running_service with the
#       X-Watchdog-Token header. This closes a boot race where
#       the watchdog's 30 s initial backoff could leave DNS
#       unavailable for minutes after boot.
#
#   The same refinements were applied in parallel to watchdog.sh
#   (§[5b] snapshot counter), status.sh (_list_snapshots),
#   customize.sh (rotate_backups), action.sh
#   (_inline_rotate_backups + _inline_backup_summary), and
#   uninstall.sh (§[5b] BACKUP_COUNT / BACKUP_LAST_NAME).
#
#   See CHANGELOG.md [v1.3.0] and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §4.13
#   for the full reference.
#
# ============================================================
# v1.4.0 — Companion Android app integration + MAIN-01
# ============================================================
#   • Optional companion Android app: `web/app-debug.apk` is
#     bundled into the module ZIP as a build artifact (fetched
#     from gasciljh/dnscrypt-proxy-app by scripts/fetch_app_apk.sh,
#     staged by .github/workflows/release.yml). It is served by
#     main.go at GET /app-debug.apk (mime:
#     application/vnd.android.package-archive, Cache-Control:
#     public, max-age=3600, immutable).
#   • WebUI install button changed: the beforeinstallprompt
#     chain introduced in v1.3.0 was REMOVED and replaced by a
#     direct `<a download>` link pointing at /app-debug.apk.
#     No browser-specific prompt logic, no beforeinstallprompt
#     dependency, no unsupported-browser modal.
#   • iOS PWA logic removed from web/index.html (Android-only
#     project): isIOSDevice(), pwaStepIos1/2/3 translations,
#     and the iOS branches in getBrowserName() /
#     isBrowserSupported() / getPWAInstallSteps() /
#     showPWAInstructionsModal().
#   • CodeQL `go/path-injection` alerts closed in main.go
#     (removeModule): sanitize via filepath.Base() + rebuild
#     the final path via filepath.Join(MODULES_DIR, name).
#     No user-controlled data reaches any path expression.
#   • MAIN-01: LOG_LEVEL is loaded immediately after
#     initPaths() in main.go, so every subsequent log call
#     respects the user's configured level. Previously the load
#     happened after readSelectedProfile() / applyMemoryLimit()
#     / getWatchdogToken() / checkPendingNotifications() /
#     cleanupOldTransactions() — those early log lines were
#     always emitted at the default "info" level.
#
# Cross-references:
#   • VERSION            — Single Source of Truth for the module
#                          version (read by scripts/release.sh)
#   • proxy/app-apk.version — Single Source of Truth for the
#                          companion Android app version (v1.4.0)
#   • update.json        — auto-update metadata (referenced by
#                          updateJson below)
#   • CHANGELOG.md       — version history (v1.0.0 → v1.4.0)
#   • docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §4.13
#                        — v1.3.0 server-side refinements
#   • docs/BACKUP.md     — backup system reference (v1.2.0)
#   • docs/EMERGENCY.md  — emergency recovery guide (v1.2.0)
#   • docs/DNS_BINARIES.md
#                        — DNS binaries management (Level 4)
#   • docs/UPGRADE.md    — version upgrade guide
#   • docs/API.md §6.1.7 — runtime_info schema (7-field backups)
#   • docs/COMPATIBILITY.md
#                        — compatibility matrix (v1.4.0)
# ============================================================

id=dnscrypt-proxy-webui
name=DNSCrypt Proxy (Smart Filter)
version=v1.4.0
versionCode=1040000
author=gasciljh
description=Smart DNS filtering with DNSCrypt. Local resolver on 127.0.0.1:5354, per-profile blocklists (HaGeZi Light → Ultimate), wildcard-aware Custom Rules, bilingual WebUI (EN/AR), JSON metrics Dashboard, atomic writes, conflict detection, Watchdog with auto-restart, nftables/iptables chains, installable PWA. v1.2.0 added 10-layer user-data preservation: multi-source detection, persistent backup in /sdcard/dnscrypt-webui-backup, SHA256 verification, transactional upgrades with auto-rollback, recovery mode, SELinux preservation, auto-backup rotation (max 21 copies), upgrade history log, and a CLI diagnose tool. v1.3.0 added a smart dynamic PWA install button and a live status LED, fixed DNS auto-start after boot, and refined backup rotation on the server side (manifest-based snapshot detection, mtime sort, protected .last_stable + newest install targets). v1.4.0 integrates an optional companion Android app (fetched separately from gasciljh/dnscrypt-proxy-app), replaces the beforeinstallprompt chain with a direct download link, hardens removeModule against CodeQL path-injection, removes iOS-specific PWA logic (Android-only project), and loads LOG_LEVEL earlier in main.go (MAIN-01). Zero telemetry.
updateJson=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gasciljh/dnscrypt-proxy-webui/main/update.json
minMagiskVersion=20400
supportUrl=https://github.com/gasciljh/dnscrypt-proxy-webui/issues
donateUrl=